        "title": "Packaging equality omits separate additions and removals to retained articles",
        "description": "The packaging-specific equality is opening+P+I+ER=closing+S+EO+W. P/I/ER are qualified whole-article receipts; the surrounding complete clauses expressly keep independently measured repair material/water changes separate and retain them in full wet closing stock. With opening pallet mass 30 kg, no whole-article receipts, dispatch/returns/waste, and 10 kg new repair material or water retained in the pallet, closing is 40 kg. The specific equality gives 30=40 despite the conserving general physical gate giving 30+10=40. Exact reconciliation against other flow terms cannot remove the required inlet from this subledger.",
        "minimum_correction": "Include independently measured, non-overlapping material/water additions on the left and removals on the right, after reconciliation with P/I/ER and S/EO/W; alternatively state an explicit equivalent restricted unchanged-article subledger and companion change balance. Preserve full wet stocks, whole-article origins and gross six legs. Apply both languages and projection.",
